        "html": "The day-to-day reality makes the difference between a township and a standalone building clear, not a brochure. In a standalone tower, the building stops at the compound wall: the gym is a single room, the open space is the driveway, and everything else belongs to the street. This arrangement works well in older, fully developed neighbourhoods. It is a quicker way to get into a locality, which is why standalone buildings are still a reasonable option for many people buying <strong>property in Thane</strong>."
